Z||000000||AusFiero||09-18-2001||09:00 AM||||Well this has probably been asked before but does a 3.8 ltr Buick engine need an adaptor plate to bolt up to a Fiero 5 speed? <BR>Are any engine mounts commercially available for this swap? <BR>What else needs to be done besides the obvious wiring, ECM and exhaust change?<P>I can get a 3.8 SC engine for a good price. Just need to know what else I am going to be up against.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||09-18-2001||09:52 AM||||Aus,<P>There is no adapter plate necessary for the FWD version of the 3800. You are correct on the wiring, that's a gimme.<BR>I know that the front mounting plate on the cradle needs an extension forward and the 3800 mount can be used. And I believe that the stock tranny mounts and locations maybe used as well. However the mounting holes on the cradle need to be elongated to mount the transmission.<BR>Also if I'm not mistaken, the flywheel (from the 2.8) needs to be modified to bolt to the 3800s crankshaft.<P>Somebody correct me if I'm incorrect on any of the above! Thanks!<P>I'm glad that you are going to resurrect the 'over done' GT!<BR>Good luck from the 'UNITED' STATES and ALL of us here~! <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||09-18-2001||10:35 AM||||Manual transmission 3800 Camaro flywheel works and needs little modification. I have also heard from various sources that Pontiac transport 3800 engine mounts work.<P><BR>JM||||reg||1
